he was one of the most powerful men in  politics but John Bercow former Speaker  of the House of Commons is under  pressure and his entry into the House of  Lords hangs in the balance  amid claims he bullied staff now Sky  News can reveal to more people are on  the verge of submitting formal  complaints after Lord Liz vane wrote to  Commons bosses on Monday those who  worked closely with him are calling for  more people to speak out he brutalized  staff in the House of Commons and  elsewhere might include myself in that  and I think he brutalized is a good word  for what he did to Lord less pain his  private secretaries they have all told  me in private moments and some of their  experiences at the hands of John Bercow  my view is that he brutalized people  I've never seen anybody in my entire  life  treat anybody as badly as John Bercow  treated regularly the people around him  bullying allegations against mr. Berko  have been made before and there is  frustration and hurt among those who say  MPs didn't do enough anybody who was  speaking out about it was the previous  speaker was in place really received a a  cold wall of silence and I speak from  personal experience myself because when  the Cox report came out I directly  challenged the speaker on the floor of  the House to consider his position which  was received with a very very difficult  response for me to deal with and clearly  it's something that other members have  experienced as well sources close to the  vetting process for new peers believe  any investigation into John backhoes  behavior could delay or potentially  prevent his membership of the House of  Lords and with one complaint already and  the potential for two more the  likelihood of that investigation only  increases mr. Barco declined to be  interviewed by Sky News today but  speaking on election night he denied all  allegations of bullying against him I've  never bullied anyone in any way to any  degree in any situation at any time  I assured a straightforward rebuttal it  is not true but those who feel wronged  by him want his peerage paused and the  claims investigated fully if John Bercow  gets a peerage now people are just going  to stare at that  in disbelief with incredulity and the  reputation of Parliament will be  traduced I think it would be a scandal  which Parliament would struggle to live  down while mr. Berko continues his life  after Parliament becoming a professor of  politics at a London University today  difficult questions remain for  parliamentary authorities both about the  past and the future - Kate McCann Sky  News
 

